{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Cross Multiplication.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Cross Multiplication.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cross multiplication cross multiplication","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Cross Multiplication.md","fileName":"Cross Multiplication.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Cross Multiplication","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Linear Equations and Modeling]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Equations and Modeling","Clearing Denominators","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Cross Multiplication.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Cross Multiplication.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cross multiplication cross multiplication","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Cross Multiplication.md","fileName":"Cross Multiplication.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Cross Multiplication","heading":"Cross Multiplication","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Cross multiplication solves a proportion by multiplying both sides by both nonzero denominators. From\n\n$$\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{c}{d},\\qquad b,d\\neq0,$$\n\nit follows that\n\n$$ad=bc.$$\n\nThe step is a shorthand for [[Clearing Denominators]], not a separate rule that applies to arbitrary sums of fractions. When a denominator contains a variable, values that make it zero must be excluded before the products are formed. Any resulting candidate should be verified in the original proportion.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Equations and Modeling","Clearing Denominators","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Cross Multiplication.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Cross Multiplication.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","so